@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Release Pipelines";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Release Pipelines in Azure DevOps help automate software deployment to different environments efficiently and securely.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- What is a Release Pipeline? -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is a Release Pipeline?</h2>
        <p>
            A Release Pipeline automates the deployment of applications across various environments such as Dev, Test, Staging, and Production. 
            It ensures consistent, reliable, and repeatable deployments with minimal manual intervention.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/release-pipeline-overview.jpg" alt="Release Pipeline Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Release Pipelines enable CI/CD workflows for automated deployments.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Key Features -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Key Features of Release Pipelines</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Multi-Stage Deployment:</strong> Deploy applications across multiple environments systematically.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Approval Gates:</strong> Ensure quality and security through manual or automated approval checks.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Artifact Management:</strong> Supports multiple artifact sources like Azure Artifacts, GitHub, and Docker.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Rollback Mechanism:</strong> Revert to a previous version if an issue occurs in production.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Integration with Monitoring:</strong> Works with Application Insights and other monitoring tools.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Setting Up a Release Pipeline -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Setting Up a Release Pipeline</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to create a release pipeline in Azure DevOps:</p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to Azure DevOps and select your project.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Go to <strong>Releases</strong> under Pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on <strong>New Release Pipeline</strong> and choose a template.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Add artifacts from a build pipeline.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Define environments such as Dev, QA, and Production.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Configure approval gates and deployment settings.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Save and trigger the release.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/release-pipeline-setup.jpg" alt="Setting Up Release Pipelines" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Setting up a release pipeline is a crucial step in automating deployments.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for Release Pipelines</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Deployment Slots:</strong> Deploy in staging before swapping to production.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate Tests:</strong> Ensure application stability with automated testing.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Rollbacks:</strong> Configure rollback strategies for failed deployments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Secrets:</strong> Store API keys and credentials securely using Azure Key Vault.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Deployments:</strong> Use logs and alerts to track deployment performance.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps Release Pipelines simplify the software deployment process by automating releases, ensuring quality, and improving efficiency. 
            Implementing best practices enhances stability and reliability across different environments.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
